# GridDefence frontend — Vite build-time environment (VITE_* only).
#
# Copy to `frontend/.env` and adjust. Vite reads env from this directory (the
# Vite root); only variables prefixed with `VITE_` are exposed to the browser
# bundle. Do not put secrets here — everything here ships to the client.
#
# See docs/architecture/engineering-map.md for the full basemap / offline model.

# --- Engineering Map basemap (Standard only) ---------------------------------
# The map ships a SINGLE Standard basemap (no Satellite/Hybrid/Terrain, no style
# selector) with an automatic NEUTRAL fallback. Rich map is the default — no
# .env needed: the Standard style ships with a governed built-in default provider
# (OpenFreeMap Liberty, OSM/ODbL, no key), so `clone → npm install → npm run dev`
# shows the rich map out of the box when the internet is reachable. When the
# Standard provider is genuinely unavailable (offline/blocked/failed), the map
# falls back to a built-in NEUTRAL reference (public-domain Natural Earth
# land/sea/coastline/borders, bundled at frontend/public/map-assets/neutral/) —
# no config, no internet, no install.
#
# Standard resolves as: VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD → VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL (legacy
# alias) → built-in default. The variable is an OPTIONAL OVERRIDE. Examples:
#
#   Connected (requires internet), a governed provider (licensing-policy §6b):
#     # OpenFreeMap (no key, OSM/ODbL, CORS; community-hosted, no SLA):
#     #   VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD=https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty
#     # MapTiler/Stadia (DOMAIN-RESTRICTED browser key; never commit a real value):
#     #   VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD=https://api.maptiler.com/maps/streets-v2/style.json?key=YOUR_RESTRICTED_KEY
#
#   Offline / internal (no internet) — the committed offline Standard package
#   (frontend/public/map-assets/standard/, optional; binaries fetched by
#   `python scripts/fetch_map_assets.py` — see DEVELOPMENT.md):
#     #   VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD=/map-assets/standard/style.json
#
# Restart the Vite dev server after changing any VITE_* value (env is read at
# startup). VITE_* are build-time, browser-exposed values — NOT secrets — but do
# not commit real provider tokens. Critical/air-gapped deployments SHOULD
# override the community default with a paid/keyed provider or the self-hosted
# offline package.
# VITE_MAP_STYLE_STANDARD=
